---
// Support page for the phux mobile apps (iOS, Android). App Store Connect
// lists it as the app's Support URL, and the apps' Info.plist SupportURL
// points here (TUIST_SUPPORT_URL in phux-mobile). Every answer describes the
// shipped app: the labels in quotes are the app's own button text in the
// phux-mobile sources. When those labels or flows change, change this page
// in the same release and bump LAST_UPDATED.
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE, docsHref } from "../lib/site";

const LAST_UPDATED = "2026-10-02";
const CONTACT = "privacy@phall.io";
const ISSUES = `${SITE.github}/issues`;
const title = `${SITE.name} — Support`;
const description =
  `How to get help with the ${SITE.name} mobile apps: pairing a server, subscriptions, your account, and how to reach us.`;
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description}>
  <article class="wrap policy">
    <header class="policy-head">
      <h1>Support</h1>
      <p class="updated">
        Last updated <time datetime={LAST_UPDATED}>{LAST_UPDATED}</time>
      </p>
      <p class="lede">
        Help with the phux mobile apps for iOS and Android, and with the phux
        server they connect to.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="summary" aria-labelledby="contact">
      <h2 id="contact">get in touch</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Email:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
          Account, subscription, and app problems all go here.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Bugs and feature requests:</strong> open an issue on
          <a href={ISSUES} target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>. Do not
          paste pairing links or tokens into an issue.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>From the app:</strong> open Settings, then "support
          diagnostics" in the SUPPORT section. You can read the redacted report
          before you send, share, or copy it. It contains no terminal content,
          server names, addresses, or tokens.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="server">
      <h2 id="server">connecting to a phux server</h2>
      <p>
        The app connects to a phux server that you install and run on your own
        Mac or Linux machine. The server is free. On Apple-silicon macOS or a
        supported Linux host, install it with Homebrew:
      </p>
      <pre><code>brew install no-phux/tap/phux</code></pre>
      <p>or with the release installer:</p>
      <pre><code>curl -fsSL https://phux.sh/install | sh</code></pre>
      <p>
        Then, on that machine, run <code>phux pair --qr</code> and scan the QR
        code from the app, or open the pairing link it prints on your phone.
        The <a href={docsHref("/quickstart/install")}>install guide</a> covers
        other platforms, and
        <a href={docsHref("/remote-access")}>remote access</a> covers reaching
        your server from outside your local network.
      </p>
      <p>
        If the app cannot connect, check that the server is running, that your
        phone can reach it on the network, and that the pairing link has not
        been revoked. Run <code>phux pair --qr</code> again for a fresh link.
        See <a href={docsHref("/troubleshooting")}>troubleshooting</a> for more.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="playground">
      <h2 id="playground">trying the app without a server</h2>
      <p>
        On the first screen, tap "open the playground". It runs a working
        terminal on your device, with no server, account, or installation.
        "don't have phux yet?" on the same screen shows the install command.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="subscription">
      <h2 id="subscription">phux Pro subscriptions</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Manage or cancel.</strong> On iOS, subscriptions are billed
        by Apple. Cancel or change your plan in the Settings app: tap your
        name, then Subscriptions, then phux. In phux, the SUBSCRIPTION section
        of Settings shows your plan and, while a subscription is active,
        offers "manage subscription", which opens Apple's subscription
        management. Cancel at
        least 24 hours before the end of the current period to avoid renewal.
        On Android, manage subscriptions in Google Play under Payments and
        subscriptions.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Restore purchases.</strong> On a new device, or after
        reinstalling, tap "upgrade to Pro" in the SUBSCRIPTION section of
        Settings, then "restore purchases". Use the same Apple Account you
        subscribed with. The app reports "purchases restored" or that no phux
        Pro purchase was found for that Apple Account.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Refunds.</strong> Apple handles refunds for App Store
        purchases. Request one at
        <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="account">
      <h2 id="account">your account</h2>
      <p>
        An account is optional. Every terminal feature works without one; an
        account only syncs your settings across devices. You can sign in with
        Apple or with a one-time code sent to your email address.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Deleting your account.</strong> Open Settings from the app
        header and, in the ACCOUNT section, tap "delete account", then confirm.
        This deletes your phux account and its synced servers and settings.
        It does not cancel an App Store subscription; cancel that as described
        above. If your app does not offer in-app deletion, email
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Exporting your data.</strong> While signed in, tap "export
        account data" in the ACCOUNT section to get everything your account
        holds as a JSON file.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="privacy">
      <h2 id="privacy">privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Your terminal traffic goes directly between your device and your own
        server and never reaches us. The <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>
        describes what the apps and services collect and how to access or
        delete it.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy {
    max-width: calc(var(--reading-width) + 2 * var(--page-gutter));
    padding-block: clamp(32px, 6vw, 72px) 96px;
  }
  .policy-head {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    padding-bottom: 24px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 40px);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
  }
  .updated {
    font-family: var(--font-code);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  .lede {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }
  section {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    padding-block: 24px;
  }
  section:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 20px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  p,
  ul {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 1.25em;
  }
  li + li {
    margin-top: 6px;
  }
  .summary {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    padding: 20px;
    margin-block: 24px;
  }
  .summary ul {
    margin: 0;
  }
  a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  a:hover,
  a:focus-visible {
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
  }
  code {
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }
  pre {
    max-width: 100%;
    overflow-x: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    padding: 12px;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
</style>
